%description:

Tcp.delayedAckFrameCount:one -- the receiver acknowledges each data segment.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "with delayedAcksEnabled, the ACK goes at once when this number of
full-sized segments waits for it, or when the unacknowledged data reach this number times
RMSS [...]; at least 1".

The classes: one (1), many (2 and more; 2 is the default), invalid (0 and less). With 1, each
full-sized segment gets its ACK at once, and the last, shorter one gets the delayed ACK
(TcpAlgorithmBase::receiveSeqChanged()). This test separates "one" from "many": with 2,
one ACK covers two segments.

Host under test: host2, the receiver. Peer: host1 sends 10000 bytes. Observation: level 1,
the ACKs without data of host2, counted, and the data segments that host2 receives, counted:
when host1 receives the ACK of the last byte, the two counts are the same.

%# parameter: Tcp.delayedAckFrameCount
%# class: one
%# value: 1
%# key: *.host2.tcp.delayedAckFrameCount
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDelayedAckFrameCountOne")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .describe("the SYN of host1")
                  .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("segments")
                                        .describe("each data segment at host2")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength == tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("acks")
                                        .describe("each ACK without data of host2")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 10001")
                  .first()
                  .assertPacket("{acks} == {segments}")
                  .describe("the ACK of the last byte at host1")
                  .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDelayedAckFrameCountOne compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.delayedAckFrameCount = 1    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDelayedAckFrameCountOne: PASS
